*Solution Steps Walkthrough:*

1. Integrate $("Log" z)/(z^2 + 9)$ along an indented semicircular contour in the upper half plane.
2. Express the integral along the negative real axis in terms of $ln t + i pi$.
3. Calculate the residue at the simple pole $z = 3 i$.
4. Equate the real parts to solve for $I = integral_0^oo (ln x)/(x^2 + 9) d x$.
